      "message": "Would it ever make sense to have `ProcessState` initialized without kernel binder support on a device? Or is it _only_ responsible for kernel binder?\n\nThere are a few places in [IServiceManager.cpp/BakcendUnifiedServiceManager.cpp](https://source.corp.google.com/search?q\u003dprocessstate::self%20f:libs%2Fbinder%20f:manager\u0026sq\u003d\u0026ss\u003dh%2Fgoogleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%2F%2B%2Frefs%2Fheads%2Fmain:frameworks%2Fnative%2Flibs%2Fbinder%2F) that call `ProcessState::Self()` and deference it immediately.\n\nI don\u0027t think we need any of the functionality from it (maybe the caching if we want to do that). So I could check `ProcessState::Self()` and change it to return nullptr instead.",
